---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import Preview from '../components/Preview.astro';

// Placeholders until real details land (see CLAUDE.md content TODOs).
const CAL = 'https://cal.com/akintayo';
const EMAIL = 'mailto:hello@akintayo.dev';
---

<Base
  title="Akintayo Akinnibosun — Frontend Developer"
  description="I build fast, accessible marketing sites for devtools companies — one person, from the first idea to the finished site."
>
  <Nav onHome />

  <main id="top">
    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Frontend developer</p>
      <h1>I build fast, accessible marketing sites <span class="mute">for devtools companies.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">One person, from the first idea to the finished site. I care about how it reads, how fast it loads, and whether everyone can use it.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <Button href="#work" variant="primary">See the work</Button>
        <Button href={CAL} variant="ghost">Book a call</Button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ WORK ============ -->
    <section class="section wrap" id="work">
      <SectionHead num="01" title="Selected work" />
      <p class="section-note">One project, told properly — not a wall of thumbnails. It's an environmental NGO, not a devtools company, but the work is the same one I'd bring to your launch site: take a slow, broken build and make it fast and accessible for the people who have to use it.</p>

      <div class="work-grid single">
        <a class="case-card" href="/work/centre-for-earthworks">
          <div class="stage">
            <Preview url="centreforearthworks.org" aspect="tall" />
          </div>
          <div class="case-meta">
            <div>
              <h3>Centre for Earthworks</h3>
              <div class="case-kind">Environmental NGO · performance + accessibility rebuild</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>An environmental NGO's site took about eleven seconds to show anything on the phones its audience actually uses. I rebuilt it to appear in two.</p>
          <span class="case-link">Read case study <span class="arrow">↗</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ HOW IT WORKS ============ -->
    <section class="section wrap" id="how">
      <SectionHead num="02" title="How it works" />
      <p class="section-note">Hiring someone for a site that matters is a gamble. Here's how it goes, so there are no surprises.</p>

      <div class="how-list">
        <div class="how-row">
          <div class="how-num">01 — A short call</div>
          <div>
            <div class="how-title">We talk it through.</div>
            <div class="how-desc">We go over what you're building and what you need. No obligation — it's how we both find out if I'm the right fit.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="how-row">
          <div class="how-num">02 — Fixed scope, fixed price</div>
          <div>
            <div class="how-title">One number, up front.</div>
            <div class="how-desc">We agree on exactly what I'm building and what it costs before I start. Most projects land in the $3–5k range.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="how-row">
          <div class="how-num">03 — Start to finish</div>
          <div>
            <div class="how-title">One person builds the whole thing.</div>
            <div class="how-desc">Nothing gets lost in a handoff. You see it as a working page early, not a mockup you have to imagine built.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="how-row">
          <div class="how-num">04 — A clear timeline</div>
          <div>
            <div class="how-title">You know the date before we start.</div>
            <div class="how-desc">Most sites ship in two to four weeks.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ ABOUT ============ -->
    <section class="section wrap" id="about">
      <SectionHead num="03" title="About" />

      <div class="about-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="about-lede">I’m a frontend developer who builds marketing sites, start to finish.</p>
          <div class="about-body">
            <p>Most devtools founders I work with are technical and short on time. You could build the site yourself — you probably did. But it ended up looking like the template it started from, and it doesn’t match the product behind it.</p>
            <p>So that’s the part I take on. I build the whole thing — the layout, the type, the responsive work — and I keep at it until it looks right. No template, no page-builder, nothing heavier than it needs to be.</p>
            <p>Most of my attention goes to two things. The first is craft — the product-minded choices about how a site works, and the small touches that bring a moment of delight when you don’t expect one. The second is whether everyone can use it. That part matters to me past the score — it’s about not leaving people out.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-tools">
            <span class="chip">HTML &amp; CSS</span>
            <span class="chip">TypeScript</span>
            <span class="chip">React</span>
            <span class="chip">Astro</span>
            <span class="chip">Motion design</span>
            <span class="chip">Accessibility</span>
            <span class="chip">Performance</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-portrait"><span class="shot-tag">portrait — Akintayo</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ EXPERIENCE ============ -->
    <section class="section wrap" id="experience">
      <SectionHead num="04" title="Experience" />

      <div class="exp-list">
        <div class="exp-row">
          <div class="exp-yr">2024 — now</div>
          <div>
            <div class="exp-role">Independent — marketing sites for devtools</div>
            <div class="exp-note">Fast, accessible sites shipped in two to four weeks</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="exp-row placeholder">
          <div class="exp-yr">————</div>
          <div>
            <div class="exp-role">Your real roles go here</div>
            <div class="exp-note">Send me your actual history and I’ll slot it in — no invented companies.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CONTACT ============ -->
    <Footer>
      <h2>Have a launch coming up?</h2>
      <p class="contact-note">If you’re building something and the site needs to catch up, get in touch. A short call is the easiest way to start — or just email me.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top: 28px;">
        <Button href={CAL} variant="primary">Book a call</Button>
        <Button href={EMAIL} variant="ghost">Email me</Button>
      </div>
    </Footer>
  </main>
</Base>
